import{_ as i,o as t,c as n,a2 as s}from"./chunks/framework.CqpfiAoK.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"Entry 487 | Dragon Rune · Historical Regression Inevitability: Civilization Collapses Once Gu Chensha Is Absent","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Entry 487 | Dragon Rune · Historical Regression Inevitability: Civilization Collapses Once Gu Chensha Is Absent","no":487,"module":2,"tags":["Myriad-Realms Benchmark","Dragon Rune","Gu Chensha","Single-Log","Civilization Collapse"],"related":["04-Anti-Predation Core Thesis","03-Symbiotic Civilization Charter","29-Symbiotic-Degree Assessment System"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"en/0487_模块2-龙符-历史倒退必然性-古尘沙缺位文明即崩溃.md","filePath":"en/0487_模块2-龙符-历史倒退必然性-古尘沙缺位文明即崩溃.md"}'),o={name:"en/0487_模块2-龙符-历史倒退必然性-古尘沙缺位文明即崩溃.md"};function a(r,e,l,h,c,u){return t(),n("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[s('<h1 id="entry-487-dragon-rune-·-historical-regression-inevitability-civilization-collapses-once-gu-chensha-is-absent" tabindex="-1">Entry 487 | Dragon Rune · Historical Regression Inevitability: Civilization Collapses Once Gu Chensha Is Absent <a class="header-anchor" href="#entry-487-dragon-rune-·-historical-regression-inevitability-civilization-collapses-once-gu-chensha-is-absent" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Entry 487 | Dragon Rune · Historical Regression Inevitability: Civilization Collapses Once Gu Chensha Is Absent&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>Module: Module 2 · Myriad-Realms Benchmark Critique Library | Series: Dragon Rune Decomposition (Entry 3) | Benchmark base: Documents 04, 03, 29</p></blockquote><h2 id="introduction-remove-the-number-one-in-history-from-the-cosmos" tabindex="-1">Introduction: remove the number-one-in-history from the cosmos <a class="header-anchor" href="#introduction-remove-the-number-one-in-history-from-the-cosmos" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Introduction: remove the number-one-in-history from the cosmos&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Heng Yuan Zhou (Myriad-Spirits Balanced-Anchor Origin Universe)&#39;s six top-level axioms — anti-predation axiom, republican axiom of Myriad Races, collective ascension axiom, causal self-discipline axiom, <strong>law-first axiom</strong>, universal equal infinite law as core — ultimate test for single-log civilization is the same thought experiment: <strong>take the protagonist out of the cosmos, what is left?</strong> Gu Chensha&#39;s answer is cruelest. The universal equal infinite law: within the Anchor Symbiotic Civilization, all beings inherently possess basic infinite power; the easygoing retain a guaranteed basic infinity and will never be eliminated; strivers and Youth Supremes can superimpose more and higher levels of infinity. Infinite origin is inherent in all, so predation naturally loses its meaning.</p><h2 id="i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" tabindex="-1">I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones <a class="header-anchor" href="#i-energy-level-waste-analysis-of-this-system-s-strong-ones" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;I. &quot;Energy-Level Waste&quot; Analysis of This System&#39;s Strong Ones&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Quest Sediment Domain fully replicates the Dragon Rune world. At Gu Chensha&#39;s peak after &quot;mending sky and reforming heaven,&quot; variable injected: Gu Chensha falls in a cross-cosmos operation, no longer exists. Observation results:</p><ul><li>Day 1: cracks appear at cosmos edge; no one can mend</li><li>Day 7: karmic backlash; Myriad Races begin cursing each other because &quot;no one bears sins&quot;</li><li>Day 30: Myriad Ranks&#39; cultivation system overall confused; no one knows &quot;Tiandao Law&#39;s next step&quot;</li><li>Day 100: cosmos begins collapsing</li></ul><p>Conclusion: Gu Chensha alone bore four cosmos-tier functions: &quot;sky-mending + sin-bearing + defining the Great Dao + maintaining order.&quot; Once he falls, four functions simultaneously vacant.</p><h2 id="ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" tabindex="-1">II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression <a class="header-anchor" href="#ii-why-this-civilization-inevits-historical-regression" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;II. Why This Civilization Inevits Historical Regression&quot;">​</a></h2><p>This is single-log civilization&#39;s ultimate fate: <strong>all of civilization&#39;s key functions concurrently held by one person.</strong> The stronger he is, the less Myriad Ranks are needed; the less Myriad Ranks are needed, the less ability they have to take over. After a thousand years, the ability gap between him and Myriad Ranks already unbridgeable — he wants Myriad Ranks to take over, but they cannot.</p><h2 id="iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" tabindex="-1">III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking <a class="header-anchor" href="#iii-deep-decomposition-of-the-protagonist-s-predatory-thinking" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;III. Deep Decomposition of the Protagonist&#39;s Predatory Thinking&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Gu Chensha&#39;s &quot;bearing sins for Myriad Ranks&quot; sounds selfless, but it structurally completes a deepest predation: <strong>he also undertook Myriad Ranks&#39; opportunity to learn to take responsibility.</strong> After a thousand years, Myriad Ranks not only cannot take over ability-wise, psychologically lost the consciousness of &quot;I need to carry it myself.&quot;</p><h2 id="iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" tabindex="-1">IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative <a class="header-anchor" href="#iv-comparison-with-anchor-symbiosis-s-complete-alternative" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;IV. Comparison With Anchor Symbiosis&#39;s Complete Alternative&quot;">​</a></h2><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Gu Chensha Single-Log</th><th>Anchor-Symbiosis Alternative</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>He alone mends sky</td><td>Myriad-Ranks co-build sky-mending project</td></tr><tr><td>He alone bears sins</td><td>Myriad Ranks bear their own karma</td></tr><tr><td>He defines the Great Dao</td><td>Great Dao public legislation</td></tr><tr><td>He maintains order</td><td>Anchor Council + Supervisory Committee</td></tr><tr><td>He falls, cosmos collapses</td><td>Distributed redundancy; any individual absence does not affect</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" tabindex="-1">V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#v-quest-sediment-domain-simulation-review-plan" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;V. Quest Sediment Domain Simulation Review Plan&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Quest Sediment Domain control: Path A = Gu Chensha single-log; Path B = Anchor-Symbiosis type. Two paths run ten thousand years: Path A collapses within five hundred years after Gu Chensha falls; Path B continues rising. <strong>Single-log civilization&#39;s lifespan is that single log&#39;s lifespan.</strong></p><p>This control also reveals a time-scale question: when Gu Chensha is alive, single-log civilization looks more &quot;brilliant&quot; than symbiotic civilization — because all energy concentrated on one person; his light outshines everything. But brilliance is unsustainable. Symbiotic civilization early looks less dazzling — because energy distributed across Myriad Ranks; no one emits that &quot;number one in history&quot; light. But distributed energy can last ten thousand, a hundred thousand, a million years; concentrated energy can only last Gu Chensha&#39;s lifespan. <strong>Short-term brilliance, and long-term survival; Heng Yuan Zhou chooses the latter.</strong></p><p>This time-scale comparison is a wake-up call for all &quot;protagonist as civilization&quot; narratives. When Gu Chensha is alive, his light makes all readers believe &quot;this cosmos will not collapse&quot; — because there is Gu Chensha. But readers forgot to ask: what if Gu Chensha is gone? A cosmos that bets all key functions on one person, no matter how great that person, its lifespan does not exceed that person&#39;s lifespan. Heng Yuan Zhou&#39;s answer: <strong>a truly great cosmos should let its greatest person also exit at peace — because the cosmos does not need him to prop it; the cosmos can run itself.</strong> Gu Chensha cannot do this, because from the start he never intended the cosmos to &quot;run itself.&quot;</p><p>Quest Sediment Domain also did a control: let Gu Chensha from the second millennium start &quot;consciously cultivating successors.&quot; Result shows: even starting cultivation from the second millennium, already too late — the first two thousand years&#39; &quot;single-person operation&quot; already made Myriad Ranks completely lose autonomous operation ability; cultivated successors are only &quot;miniature Gu Chensha,&quot; still single-log. <strong>Single-log civilization&#39;s irreversibility is that it cannot cultivate forest — it can only cultivate more single logs.</strong> What Heng Yuan Zhou wants is not &quot;cultivate successors,&quot; but &quot;build forest from the start.&quot;</p><p>This conclusion is a wake-up call for all single-log civilizations: Gu Chensha is not not great enough, he is too great — so great that Myriad Ranks do not need to grow on their own.</p><h2 id="vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" tabindex="-1">VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment <a class="header-anchor" href="#vi-setting-self-consistency-retcon-ending-risk-assessment" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;VI. Setting Self-Consistency / Retcon-Ending Risk Assessment&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Setting self-consistency: medium-low</strong>. Cosmos survival tied to one person itself not self-consistent under civilizational logic</li><li><strong>Retcon-ending risk: high</strong></li><li><strong>Protagonist uniqueness dependency: extremely high</strong> (single-log ceiling)</li></ul><p><strong>Old-new cosmos resource comparison</strong>: old-cosmos resources and Great Dao are finite, inevitably predatory involution; Anchor Symbiosis has everyone inherently possessing infinite origin, predation loses meaning.</p><h2 id="five-core-takeaways" tabindex="-1">Five Core Takeaways <a class="header-anchor" href="#five-core-takeaways" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Five Core Takeaways&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Anti-energy waste</strong>: four cosmos functions on one person</li><li><strong>Anti-predation</strong>: even Myriad Ranks&#39; chance to take responsibility is &quot;undertaken&quot;</li><li><strong>Tang-Luo upper-limit comparison</strong>: Tang Luo at least let students cultivate independently; Gu Chensha does not let Myriad Ranks be independent</li><li><strong>Myriad Races full coverage</strong>: Myriad Ranks nominally &quot;all can become dragons,&quot; actually no one can carry</li><li><strong>Hyper-multiverse full openness</strong>: single-log cosmos farthest from network type</li><li><strong>Universal equal infinite law</strong>: basic infinite power inherent in all; easygoing retain guarantee, strivers can superimpose higher; infinite origin eliminates predation motive</li></ul><h2 id="conclusion" tabindex="-1">Conclusion <a class="header-anchor" href="#conclusion" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Conclusion&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The day Gu Chensha falls, the cosmos falls with him. This is not because the cosmos is fragile, but because it was never a cosmos — it is Gu Chensha&#39;s shadow. <strong>Shadows cannot leave the person.</strong></p><p>In the final analysis, Dragon Rune · historical regression inevitability · civilization collapses once Gu Chensha is absent described in this document is no isolated case — its causality and energy-level traces are filed throughout in the Alaya Network, traceable and verifiable.</p><h2 id="related" tabindex="-1">Related <a class="header-anchor" href="#related" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Related&quot;">​</a></h2><ul><li>Related documents: <a href="./485_模块2-龙符-总论古尘沙与独木式文明定性.html">Entry 485 · Overview</a> · <a href="./488_模块2-龙符-古尘沙掠夺思维拆解-替众生承罪的恩赐本质.html">Entry 488 · Gu Chensha&#39;s Predatory Thinking</a> · <a href="./../wanling-hengmao-origin-universe-archive/docs/zh/03-共生文明宪章.html">03-Symbiotic Civilization Charter</a></li><li>Official site: <a href="https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://faker210.github.io/hengyuan-cosmos/zh/</a></li></ul>',30)])])}const m=i(o,[["render",a]]);export{g as __pageData,m as default};
